"Simon" <yaroguelike@googlemail.com> wrote:
> Haakon Studebaker wrote:
>
>> Okay six days short of three years and still no new NetHack.
>>
>> What are your speculations for the new NetHack... IF there's going to be
>> another release (3.5.0, 4.0, etc).
>
> One thought occurred to me - perhaps the DevTeam got fed up with the
> horrendous codebase and are producing a nice, clean, simple, easy to
> maintain rewrite that everyone can understand.

Considering how long NetHack has been in development and how much code
has been written I don't think it is that horrendous. Of course it
could be better but I doubt that a complete rewrite would be better.

What I'm missing is a little more granularity in the code and a little
more modern development features.

E.g. the wishing code is one big fat procedure. This is not
nice-looking code.

Something like unittests would be really helpful. Sometimes you're
looking at the code, change something and pray to $NETHACKGOD that you
didn't break something. With unittests you would know if you broke
something.

> That could easily take 3 years!

Or maybe more ...

